    fn __security_init_cookie();
    fn __security_check_cookie(cookie: *const core::ffi::c_void);
    fn __report_gsfailure(reason: u32) -> !;
}
```

These stubs are provided by the verification harness. Your function code then calls
them through the extern block — the body is a no-op during verification.

### 3. Internal DLL functions
Functions like `dllmain_dispatch` or any function that is defined inside the target
DLL (not a Windows API or CRT function) are **not available** to the compiled stub.
Declare them as extern stubs alongside the CRT internals:

```rust
extern "C" {
    fn dllmain_dispatch(hinst: *mut core::ffi::c_void, fdw_reason: u32, reserved: *mut core::ffi::c_void);
}
```

### 4. Self-translated functions in the same DLL
If function A calls function B and both belong to the same project DLL, declare B
as an extern stub. It will be translated independently and linked at restitch time:

```rust
extern "C" {
    fn helper_compute_x(x: i32, y: i32) -> i32;
}
```

